262
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,468
You're my best friend, too.

263
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:56,700
Goodbye, Ken.

264
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:03,900
Wormmon, no!

265
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,800
He's gone, Ken.

266
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,620
He can't be!

267
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,560
Not again.

268
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,920
Wormmon's gone.

269
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:19,520
Just like my brother.

270
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:24,026
I was helpless to save him, and
now I can't save Wormon either.

271
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:29,080
Why do I keep losing people?

272
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:33,077
I came to the digital world to
get away from all those feelings,

273
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,572
but I just can't escape.

274
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,300
Can we miss you?

275
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,880
There's still people who love you.

276
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,920
I gotta go

277
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,895
Don't walk away from your
problems Let us help you, Ken

278
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:02,000
You're Digi-Destin Join us

279
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:06,700
I wonder where he's going
I hope you'll be okay

280
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,500
Hey, Matt I made it

281
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:16,397
Oh, no, she followed us.

282
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:18,257
She's like a boomerang
that keeps coming back.

283
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,617
It's funny, but when you drove
off with your tires screeching,

284
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,997
you didn't realize you
left me standing there.

285
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,940
My bad. Sorry about that.

286
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:26,298
I must have forgot.

287
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,879
Oh, where are Davis and the others?

288
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:32,220
I think Tai knows.

289
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:34,197
Hey, Tai, do you know
where the others went?

290
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,280
Let me think about that for a sec.

291
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:39,225
Uh, Izzy, weren't you
the last one to see them?

292
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,440
Of course.

293
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:44,288
I'll go find him right now.

294
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,320
Oh, boy, what am I supposed to do?

295
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:56,600
The digiport is opening.

296
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:03,880
Did you guys hear that noise?

297
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,940
It could be a wild animal.

298
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:08,077
Yeah, the woods are a dangerous place.

299
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,417
Davis, you better leave quick.

300
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:11,820
I'll tell Davis you stopped by. How?

301
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:15,960
There they are.

302
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:19,500
Hey, June, who invited you
to come out here? Matt did.

303
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:23,240
Hey, guys, wait for me.

304
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:26,080
That was a close one.

305
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:29,277
Hey, would it be okay to get
a ride home with you guys?

306
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:31,097
I don't want to take
the bus all by myself.

307
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,977
No way, not in a million years.

308
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:33,890
Take the bus.

309
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:36,804
It's not my fault you
came all the way out here.

310
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,620
It's not fair.

311
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:40,880
Come on, kids.

312
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:41,910
That's not nice.

313
00:19:41,993 --> 00:19:43,577
Someone take the bus with June.

314
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:47,877
That's very nice of you, sir, and I
already have the perfect volunteer in mind.

315
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,620
And the absolute perfect volunteer is TK.

316
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:53,340
Matt, you take the bus
home with June. Huh?

317
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:54,680
I'm broke.

318
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,665
There's more than enough here.

319
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,160
Have fun, you two.

320
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:00,167
Have her home before curfew.

321
00:20:01,260 --> 00:20:02,731
I'll trade for your seat.

322
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:04,480
Don't be silly.

323
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:05,698
You'll sit with me.

324
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,660
Come on, hunk.

325
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,428
We better go catch the bus.

326
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:11,477
It's a long ride.

327
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:13,757
Please, TK, you can have my college money.

328
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:14,670
Bye.

329
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,440
See you in four hours.

330
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:21,700
I give up.

331
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:25,077
And in local news, the missing
boy genius, Ken Ichichoji,

332
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:28,357
mysteriously returned home after being
missing for the last several months.

333
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,077
Events surrounding his
puzzling disappearance

334
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:32,257
and sudden reappearance are still unclear,

335
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:36,500
but his family is thankful to have
him home and safe. Good day. Well,

336
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,137
looks like the Digi world will be a safer

337
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:40,437
place from now on without
Ken running the show.

338
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:44,108
Yeah, that sure must have been
some battle these guys fought.

339
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,697
I think we older kids
can take a lot of pride

340
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:49,757
when we call these beginners
the new Digi Destined.

341
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:50,837
You're right, Izzy.

342
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:54,391
The torch has been passed, and
they didn't get burned once.

343
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,300
My little boy is back.

344
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:03,437
First we lost his
brother, then we lost Ken.

345
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:05,840
I'm just so glad he's back home.

346
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:40,340
I'm gonna be like, I'll be
like, I'm gonna be all good.

347
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:43,054
I'm gonna be all good.

348
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:48,837
I'm gonna

349
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:52,520
be all good.

350
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:22,920
Go Just Now

351
00:22:49,300 --> 00:22:51,006
We will start with the V-mon.

352
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:55,420
We will start the next episode
of the Digimon Adventure Zero 2.

353
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,740
Go U .S. V-mon.

354
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:00,260
Now, the gate is open.
